 "title": "Cryptococcus neoformans and its associated proteases and virulence factors",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around Cryptococcus neoformans, an organism that expresses Kex2p, a protease, and has various virulence factors such as laccase, melanin production, polysaccharide capsule, and urease. The organism also interacts with the influenza virus. Kex2p is associated with the Golgi apparatus and cleaves hemagglutinin glycoproteins, including those of the H5N1 influenza virus. The cluster also includes various methods and tools used in proteomics and mass spectrometry, such as MaxQuant, HADDOCK, and timsTOF Pro 2 mass spectrometer.",
